From: Saphira packaging <recipes@saphira.vm2.uk>
Subject: [PATCH] gcc15+: mark imsm_orom.signature nonstring

The "$VER"/"$NVM"/"$VMD" tags are 4-byte OROM magic compared with
memcmp(): the truncated NUL is intentional. Tell gcc so with the
nonstring field attribute instead of weakening -Werror (one
attribute fixes all three initializer sites).

--- a/platform-intel.h
+++ b/platform-intel.h
@@ -27,1 +27,1 @@
-	__u8 signature[4];
+	__u8 signature[4] __attribute__((nonstring));
